  ],
  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "bobble"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "bobble"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " sits lower and denser than a popcorn — it pushes forward on the public face without requiring the hook removal step, which makes it faster to work in long runs. This square places one bobble at the centre of each side on rounds 3 and 5, with "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "treble-cluster"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "treble clusters"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " either side of each bobble. The dense texture suits pot holders and cushion covers where structure matters. Start from a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " to keep the centre hole closed. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "blocking"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Blocking"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " flattens the background without collapsing the bobbles."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "type": "materials"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Yarn: DK cotton, approx 40 m per square. Hook: 4 mm. Notions: tapestry needle, scissors."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "12 × 12 cm in DK cotton on a 4 mm hook. The bobble rounds draw in slightly — check after round 3 and loosen hook tension if the square is smaller than 7 cm at that point."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Magic ring"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Chain (ch)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Treble (tr)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "3-treble cluster (3tr cl)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "5-treble bobble: 5 tr into same sp, joined through all loops"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Slip stitch (sl st)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 3 at the start of each round counts as the first tr throughout. Corners throughout: (3tr cl, ch 2, 3tr cl)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 1"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make a magic ring. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). 2 tr, ch 2. *(3 tr, ch 2); repeat from * 2 more times. Sl st to top of ch-3. Pull tail. (12 tr, 4 ch-2 corners)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 2"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into corner sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). (2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in corner sp. Ch 1. *(3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in next corner sp. Ch 1; repeat from * 2 more times. Sl st to top of ch-3. (24 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 4 ch-1 side sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 3 — first bobble round"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into corner sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). (2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in corner sp. Ch 1. *3 tr in ch-1 side sp. Ch 1. Work bobble (5 tr into same sp, join through all loops) in next position. Ch 1. 3 tr in next sp. Ch 1. (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in corner sp. Ch 1; repeat from * 2 more times. Sl st to top of ch-3. (4 bobbles, 36 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 12 ch-1 sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 4"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into corner sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). (2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in corner sp. Ch 1. *3 tr in each ch-1 sp across side, ch 1 between groups. (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in corner sp. Ch 1; repeat from * 2 more times. Sl st to top of ch-3. (48 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 16 ch-1 side sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 5 — second bobble round"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sl st into corner sp. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). (2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in corner sp. Ch 1. *Work clusters across side until centre sp. Work bobble in centre ch-1 sp of each side. Ch 1. Continue clusters to corner. (3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr) in corner sp. Ch 1; repeat from * 2 more times. Sl st to top of ch-3. Fasten off. (4 bobbles, 60 tr, 4 ch-2 corners, 20 ch-1 side sps)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chart"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "craftChart",
        "attrs": {
          "roundCount": 5
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in ends. Wet-block to 12 × 12 cm. The bobble rounds pull in slightly more than the cluster rounds — a longer soak (15 minutes) and firm pinning will bring the square to its target size. Leave until fully dry."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Joining"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Join with the flat slip-stitch method through corresponding chain-1 spaces. The bobbles face outward and are not flattened by the joining seam."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine wash at 30 degrees on a gentle cycle. Reshape while damp, pushing the bobbles back to their forward position. Dry flat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work bobbles in every side position on round 3 (instead of just the centre) for a fully textured side panel. Or try replacing the corner clusters with bobbles on round 5 for a contrasting corner detail."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}